        en: 'The interpreter is a smart, lazy employee: it stops working the moment it knows the answer. Ask it “are the doors open, and is there an earthquake in the kitchen?” — answer the doors are closed, and it never enters the kitchen. This early stopping is called short-circuit evaluation — and with it you write a brilliant protection called the guardian pattern.',
      },
