        en: 'It quietly prints False: x >= 2 is false, and that is enough — and knows the answer is False no matter what follows, so it never evaluates the division. This is short-circuiting, straight from our book (p.49). But stay alert: in a moment we will see when this guardian works and when it fails embarrassingly.',
      },
