        en: 'First case: the guardian holds, the division is safe, the answer is True. Second: the guardian fails and stops evaluation before the division — False, no explosion. Third: the guardian passes, so the interpreter walks into division by zero and it blows — without last lesson’s try/except the program would have crashed. Try the right guardian in the sandbox: y != 0 and (x / y) > 2 with the same values.',
